From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrew Gazelka <andrew@ix.dev>
Date: Sat, 18 Jul 2026 22:11:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] submodule--helper: borrow common-dir module store in linked
 worktrees

A linked worktree resolves submodule gitdirs to a per-worktree path
($GIT_DIR/modules/<name>; "modules" is deliberately absent from
common_list[] so each worktree can check submodules out at different
revisions), so the first `git submodule update --init` in every new
worktree re-clones each submodule from its remote even though
$GIT_COMMON_DIR/modules/<name> already holds a complete object store.
df56607dff2 (git-common-dir: make "modules/" per-working-directory
directory, 2014-12-01) called the reuse "logical" but never
implemented it.

This bit us hard in day-to-day work: our workflow creates a git
worktree per task, and superprojects with submodules paid a full
network re-download plus a duplicated on-disk object store for every
single worktree (measured: a 5 MB submodule costs 5.0 MB disk and a
full refetch per worktree; with the fix, 112 KB and no fetch).

Teach prepare_possible_alternates() to add
$GIT_COMMON_DIR/modules/<name>/objects as a clone reference with
--reference-if-able semantics whenever the resolved submodule gitdir
is per-worktree: immutable objects are shared, per-checkout state
(HEAD, index) stays private. When the common-dir store is absent or
invalid the clone proceeds exactly as before.

Refs indexable-inc/index#3610

diff --git a/builtin/submodule--helper.c b/builtin/submodule--helper.c
index 2f589e3..ca2c0e5 100644
--- a/builtin/submodule--helper.c
+++ b/builtin/submodule--helper.c
@@ -1824,12 +1824,57 @@ static int add_possible_reference_from_superproject(
 	return 0;
 }
 
+/*
+ * A linked worktree resolves submodule gitdirs to a per-worktree
+ * location ($GIT_DIR/modules/<name>), so the first "git submodule
+ * update" in each new worktree used to re-clone every submodule from
+ * its remote even though the main checkout already holds a complete
+ * object store at $GIT_COMMON_DIR/modules/<name>. Borrow that store
+ * as an alternate when it exists and is valid ("--reference-if-able"
+ * semantics); per-worktree state (HEAD, index) stays private, which
+ * is the sharing df56607dff2 (git-common-dir: make "modules/"
+ * per-working-directory directory, 2014-12-01) anticipated but never
+ * implemented.
+ */
+static void add_possible_reference_from_common_dir(const char *sm_name,
+		struct string_list *reference)
+{
+	struct strbuf sb = STRBUF_INIT;
+	struct strbuf err = STRBUF_INIT;
+	char *sm_alternate;
+
+	if (!strcmp(repo_get_git_dir(the_repository),
+		    repo_get_common_dir(the_repository)))
+		goto done;
+
+	/*
+	 * End the path with '/' to mark it as a dir, matching
+	 * add_possible_reference_from_superproject().
+	 */
+	strbuf_addf(&sb, "%s/modules/%s/",
+		    repo_get_common_dir(the_repository), sm_name);
+
+	sm_alternate = compute_alternate_path(sb.buf, &err);
+	if (sm_alternate) {
+		char *p = strbuf_detach(&sb, NULL);
+
+		string_list_append(reference, p)->util = p;
+		free(sm_alternate);
+	}
+
+done:
+	strbuf_release(&err);
+	strbuf_release(&sb);
+}
+
 static void prepare_possible_alternates(const char *sm_name,
 		struct string_list *reference)
 {
 	char *sm_alternate = NULL, *error_strategy = NULL;
 	struct submodule_alternate_setup sas = SUBMODULE_ALTERNATE_SETUP_INIT;
 
+	add_possible_reference_from_common_dir(sm_name, reference);
+
 	repo_config_get_string(the_repository, "submodule.alternateLocation", &sm_alternate);
 	if (!sm_alternate)
 		return;
diff --git a/t/t2405-worktree-submodule.sh b/t/t2405-worktree-submodule.sh
index 11018f3..5bbbce0 100755
--- a/t/t2405-worktree-submodule.sh
+++ b/t/t2405-worktree-submodule.sh
@@ -91,4 +91,22 @@ test_expect_success 'unsetting core.worktree does not prevent running commands d
 	git -C main/.git/worktrees/checkout-recurse/modules/sub log
 '
 
+test_expect_success 'submodule update in linked worktree borrows common-dir module store' '
+	git -C main worktree add "$base_path/worktree-borrow" &&
+	git -C worktree-borrow submodule update --init &&
+	alternates="$(git -C worktree-borrow/sub rev-parse --git-path objects/info/alternates)" &&
+	test -f "$alternates" &&
+	grep "modules/sub/objects" "$alternates"
+'
+
+test_expect_success 'submodule update in linked worktree still clones without a common-dir store' '
+	git clone "$base_path/origin/main" fresh &&
+	git -C fresh worktree add "$base_path/fresh-worktree" &&
+	git -C fresh-worktree submodule update --init &&
+	alternates="$(git -C fresh-worktree/sub rev-parse --git-path objects/info/alternates)" &&
+	test ! -f "$alternates" &&
+	git -C fresh-worktree diff --submodule main"^!" >out &&
+	grep "file1 updated" out
+'
+
 test_done
